meta {
  name: 21 - Projects Incremental Sweep
  type: graphql
  seq: 21
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}
  body: graphql
  auth: inherit
}

body:graphql {
  query ProjectsIncrementalSweep {
    projects(
      first: 250
      includeArchived: true
      sort: [{updatedAt: {order: Ascending}}]
      filter: {updatedAt: {gt: "2026-07-30T00:00:00Z"}}
    ) {
      nodes { id updatedAt archivedAt }
      pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Reference: https://linear.app/developers/filtering

  The exact incremental query the connector will issue for Projects. Identical in shape to
  `11 - Issues Ascending Sweep`'s `updatedAsc` alias, differing only in the root field name
  and the filter input type (`ProjectFilter` vs `IssueFilter`) — which is the whole point
  of the cluster: one parametrized fetcher, four call sites.

  `ProjectFilter.updatedAt` exposes the same `DateComparator` (`gt`/`gte`/`lt`/`lte`/`eq`/
  `neq`/`in`/`nin`/`null`) as `IssueFilter.updatedAt`, verified by introspection.

  **Limitation / observed finding** (2026-08-04, after `Seeding/A1`): returns **1 row** —
  the seeded project, whose `updatedAt` is well after the `2026-07-30` filter bound. This
  confirms `ProjectFilter.updatedAt` and `sort` are accepted AND that the query returns real
  rows through them.

  Note what this still does NOT show: a filter bound that EXCLUDES some rows while including
  others. With a single project in the workspace, any bound below its `updatedAt` returns
  1 row and any bound above returns 0. True partial narrowing on this stream remains
  unobserved; the `gte` boundary semantics are carried over from
  `07 - Cursor Filter Boundary`, which established them on Issues against the same shared
  `DateComparator` implementation.
}

example {
  name: 200 — updatedAt filter + sort accepted, 1 row

  request: {
    url: https://api.linear.app/graphql
    method: POST
    mode: graphql

    body:graphql: {
      query ProjectsIncrementalSweep {
        projects(
          first: 250
          includeArchived: true
          sort: [{updatedAt: {order: Ascending}}]
          filter: {updatedAt: {gt: "2026-07-30T00:00:00Z"}}
        ) {
          nodes { id updatedAt archivedAt }
          pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
        }
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    headers: {
      x-complexity: 625
      x-ratelimit-requests-limit: 2500
      x-ratelimit-requests-remaining: 2484
      x-ratelimit-complexity-limit: 3000000
      x-ratelimit-complexity-remaining: 2999375
    }

    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }

    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "projects": {
              "count": 1,
              "rows": [
                {
                  "id": "1904e338-af08-4cbb-aacd-033e8845e3c0",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-08-04T18:35:04.021Z",
                  "archivedAt": null
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
